(7479629, 1189309, 50864, '<td valign="top">Interesting and fun way to take advantage of the HDR challenge. Inspiring.</td>', 'Interesting and fun way to take advantage of the HDR challenge. Inspiring.', '2016-10-26 14:32:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481089, 1189301, 115814, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the Blue, Nikki. I''m commenting here as part of the Post Challenge Volunteer thread activities. <br/> <br/>I''m generally not a fan of extreme HDR images that go beyond tone-mapping to stylized processing. For me, this shot sits right on the edge of enough vs. too much. I scored it in the top 3rd of entries, but not among my favorites. Here''s why:<br/> <br/>The lines and subject matter are terrific - nature verging on abstract. The tonal range is good with details at every level of bright/dark, but as a result, the image lacks contrast. The brightest spot on the image is on the left side between the dark clouds and the hills. My eye is drawn to a hole in the sky. I''m also not a fan of the blue/indigo cast in the clouds, I''d be curious what warming up the tones in the skies would do. <br/> <br/>This is obviously a minority opinion based on the blue ribbon and terrific score. If I were you, I''d completely ignore my comment and revel in the accolades. It''s a lovely image that I might have processed a bit differently. I pretty certain it would have scored lower, too!</td>', 'Congrats on the Blue, Nikki. I''m commenting here as part of the Post Challenge Volunteer thread activities.  I''m generally not a fan of extreme HDR images that go beyond tone-mapping to stylized processing. For me, this shot sits right on the edge of enough vs. too much. I scored it in the top 3rd of entries, but not among my favorites. Here''s why: The lines and subject matter are terrific - nature verging on abstract. The tonal range is good with details at every level of bright/dark, but as a result, the image lacks contrast. The brightest spot on the image is on the left side between the dark clouds and the hills. My eye is drawn to a hole in the sky. I''m also not a fan of the blue/indigo cast in the clouds, I''d be curious what warming up the tones in the skies would do.  This is obviously a minority opinion based on the blue ribbon and terrific score. If I were you, I''d completely ignore my comment and revel in the accolades. It''s a lovely image that I might have processed a bit differently. I pretty certain it would have scored lower, too!', '2016-11-05 14:01:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481189, 1189247, 68504, '<td valign="top">here it is the light and not the processing that blesses and gathers.</td>', 'here it is the light and not the processing that blesses and gathers.', '2016-11-06 14:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481203, 1189247, 124815, '<td valign="top">This is like a mirage.<br/>and if this is HDR i''ll try my best with it also since this image gives me hope.</td>', 'This is like a mirage.and if this is HDR i''ll try my best with it also since this image gives me hope.', '2016-11-06 18:04:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7481228, 1189301, 138630, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1190242" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/138630/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1190242.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/138630/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1190242.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/138630/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1190242.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Here''s a new edit - warmer sky, more contrast in land.<br/> <br/>Thanks so much, Bill, for the thoughtful critique.  I am probably pretty much with you on HDR images - I tried to stop short of going over the top as I really don''t like that.  I know I always process the skies separately as they always seem more problematic to me.  <br/> <br/>I did warm the earth and cool the sky - perhaps I over-did it but I really don''t like skies with a yellow cast and the sky that day had that menacing dark blue color that immediately precedes a thunderstorm in the Midwest, Southwest, or West so I tried to get rid of it, possibly erring in that direction.  I don''t mind the tones, though.<br/> <br/>Your comment about tonal range and contrast actually interests me more.  I''m still feeling the scene falls a bit flat.  I think you are suggesting I up the contrast to see what that does.  I''ll try, but I''d love more input.<br/> <br/>Sorry it took so long for me to respond beyond the "like comment" check, but we have our granddaughter for the weekend every other week and this was the one - I spend almost all my free time enjoying her :)  (And yes, she''s hopelessly spoiled.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2016-11-06 20:37:44.</i></td>', '  Here''s a new edit - warmer sky, more contrast in land. Thanks so much, Bill, for the thoughtful critique.  I am probably pretty much with you on HDR images - I tried to stop short of going over the top as I really don''t like that.  I know I always process the skies separately as they always seem more problematic to me.   I did warm the earth and cool the sky - perhaps I over-did it but I really don''t like skies with a yellow cast and the sky that day had that menacing dark blue color that immediately precedes a thunderstorm in the Midwest, Southwest, or West so I tried to get rid of it, possibly erring in that direction.  I don''t mind the tones, though. Your comment about tonal range and contrast actually interests me more.  I''m still feeling the scene falls a bit flat.  I think you are suggesting I up the contrast to see what that does.  I''ll try, but I''d love more input. Sorry it took so long for me to respond beyond the "like comment" check, but we have our granddaughter for the weekend every other week and this was the one - I spend almost all my free time enjoying her :)  (And yes, she''s hopelessly spoiled.)', '2016-11-06 20:23:30.000000', '2016-11-06 20:37:44.000000', 0),
(7481244, 1188688, 115814, '<td valign="top">Wow. What a spectacular scene! And I really appreciate the vivid, rich colors presented here without radioactive saturation. The yellow and greens seem completely authentic - refreshingly so. In the spirit of that authenticity, I might have toned down the deepest blues in the sky, but then again, it''s been a long time since I''ve been in the Rockies in the fall. Gorgeous!</td>', 'Wow. What a spectacular scene! And I really appreciate the vivid, rich colors presented here without radioactive saturation. The yellow and greens seem completely authentic - refreshingly so. In the spirit of that authenticity, I might have toned down the deepest blues in the sky, but then again, it''s been a long time since I''ve been in the Rockies in the fall. Gorgeous!', '2016-11-06 22:59:59.000000', NULL, 0),
